il_1782_RMG_BHC0444.jpg/500px-The_Battle_of_the_Saints%2C_12_April_1782_RMG_BHC0444.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Battle of the Saintes between British and French fleets in 1782, by Nicholas Pocock","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Battle_of_the_Saints%2C_12_April_1782_RMG_BHC0444.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Attack_near_Playa_Giron._April_19%2C_1961._-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Attack_near_Playa_Giron._April_19%2C_1961._-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Attack_near_Playa_Giron._April_19%2C_1961._-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Attack_near_Playa_Giron._April_19%2C_1961._-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Counter-attack by Cuban Revolutionary Armed Forces supported by T-34 tanks near Playa Giron during the Bay of Pigs Invasion, 19 April 1961.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAttack_near_Playa_Giron._April_19%2C_1961._-_panoramio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Tectonic_plates_Caribbean.png/500px-Tectonic_plates_Caribbean.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Tectonic_plates_Caribbean.png/500px-Tectonic_plates_Caribbean.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":".mw-parser-output .legend{page-break-inside:avoid;break-inside:avoid-column}.mw-parser-output .legend-color{display:inline-block;min-width:1.25em;height:1.25em;line-height:1.25;margin:1px 0;text-align:center;border:1px solid black;background-color:transparent;color:black}.mw-parser-output .legend-text{}  The Caribbean plate is the reason islands exist here. On the north, obduction has scraped rocks onto the North American plate (such as in western Cuba). On the east, the Lesser Antilles subduction zone produces volcanism and an island arc. Complex interactions with the South American plate has created islands along the southern boundary. Coral islands are found in insular Colombia near the east coast of Central America.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATectonic_plates_Caribbean.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Johny_Cay.jpg/500px-Johny_Cay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Johny_Cay.jpg/1280px-Johny_Cay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Johny_Cay.jpg/500px-Johny_Cay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tropical monsoon climate in San Andrés island, Caribbean, Colombia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohny_Cay.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Tobacco_field_cuba1.jpg/500px-Tobacco_field_cuba1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Tobacco_field_cuba1.jpg/500px-Tobacco_field_cuba1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A field in Pinar del Rio planted with Cuban tobacco","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATobacco_field_cuba1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Jayuya.jpg/500px-Jayuya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Jayuya.jpg/1280px-Jayuya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Jayuya.jpg/500px-Jayuya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm